title scooter_input -- the typed keeper: raw keystroke bytes drive a session to the journal, GREEN
prompt recur: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Season G terminal family; send often; deep-read one council-rota doc; stop at custody gates.
think The prior lap (dexter_key) closed the byte-to-key floor and its own recommend named this exact crux: wire drive() to scooter_compose.Session. Two proven halves stood a step apart -- dexter_key.drive edits a dexter_line and stops at Enter; scooter_compose.Session.prompt() IS that line and submit() commits it. The join is pure, bounded, no gate: the highest-Lindy crux among agent-doable work, closing the write loop from raw keystroke bytes all the way to the journal.
think Council rota deep-read this lap: foundations/20260810-011514_pond-the-application-module.md -- Pond is the floor where modules compose into a running whole a person holds; Scooter is an app in Pond, customs governs receipt at the serve seam. Kept the network wire (Comlink between Constel piers) as the maintainer's serve gate, exactly where this pure rung stops.
think Held scooter_input owning no line of its own -- it drives the session's own prompt through dexter_key over the same bounded API, so dexter_line enforces every edit bound in one place. feed walks the run; each drive advances 1+ bytes so the loop terminates; on a decoded Enter, submit commits, counting only a real post via the returned seq, tolerating EmptyEntry (a blank Enter posts nothing), and stopping the feed by name on JournalFull with the bytes consumed so a caller resumes the remainder rather than dropping keystrokes.
obs Two reds, both caught by the witness on metal, neither a design flaw. First: the full-journal test asserted used < 10, but the failing line "lost\n" was last, so used equalled the whole 10-byte run -- the feed consumes the Enter before the submit it triggers fails. Fixed by trailing the run with "more\n" (15 bytes) and asserting used == 10, proving the early stop leaves the tail untouched. Second: the determinism run "gr ESC[D ai ESC[F n" spelled "gairn", not "grain" (a Left+insert lands the bytes between g and r); replaced with "rain ESC[H g" which genuinely yields "grain" and exercises Home too.
obs First posted-count draft guarded on s.line.len == 0 after submit, which an empty Enter also satisfies -- it would have miscounted blanks as posts. Fixed to count on submit's success return (a seq) before running the witness, so EmptyEntry and JournalFull are handled by name and only a real post increments.
obs tame_style_check bans clean (my file carries many asserts, not on the zero-assert list), width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, >=2 positive // invariant asserts per fn, one seam @intCast on bytes.len after the bound assert proves it fits u32.
loom witness=scooter_input_witness cruxes=6 max_feed=4096 max_posts=256 green=first-run-after-two-witness-reds
file pond/apps/scooter_input.rye the typed-keeper loop: feed(session, bytes) drives the prompt through dexter_key and submits on Enter; Feed{stop, posted, used}; selftest proves the six cruxes
file tools/scooter_input_witness.rish builds the module and asserts GREEN over the six cruxes; no TTY, no key, no funds
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge + Git nib refreshed to the typed-keeper write loop; prior nib demoted
recommend keep-going the pure write loop stands whole from keyboard bytes to the journal; the next rungs -- the raw TTY read (cbreak, escape timing) and the Comlink wire between two Constel piers -- reach the serve gate, the maintainer's hand, so the next agent-doable Lindy crux is the READ side: fold a keeper's freshly typed post back into the drawn frame live (scooter_paint over a fed session), or open the open-fonts journey the media family still wants.
